# Nothing a build needs that isn't package.json/lock + src. Keeping the context
# small also keeps any stray local secret file out of the build context.
#
# Defence in depth rather than the only control: the Dockerfile COPYs the package
# files, the tsconfigs and src/ by name, so nothing else reaches an image even if
# it reaches the context. The patterns below are here because "excludes
# config.json" is not the promise this header makes. A local .env or a test
# keypair went to the daemon regardless, and would land in any image the day a
# broader COPY is added.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.git/
.github/
docs/
config.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.log
.eslintrc*